IO-60: report a 0 % LID continuity error for a unit with no water

lid_writeWaterBalance() set the error to 100 % whenever a unit's initial
storage plus inflow was zero, so a LID unit that received nothing and held
nothing (dry period, no contributing area) was reported with a 100 %
continuity error although its balance is exactly zero. Report 0 % in that
case, and -100 % if such a unit somehow had outflow, the value the system
continuity tables (massbal.c) give for outflow without inflow.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-60_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
index e2ac45a..eacc874 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
@@ -2003,7 +2003,7 @@ void lid_writeWaterBalance()
                       lidUnit->waterBalance.surfFlow +
                       lidUnit->waterBalance.drainFlow;
             if ( inflow > 0.0 ) err = (inflow - outflow) / inflow;
-            else                err = 1.0;
+            else                err = (outflow > 0.0) ? -1.0 : 0.0;
             fprintf(Frpt.file, "  %10.2f", err*100.0);
             lidList = lidList->nextLidUnit;
         }
